  "description": "The precision rule shared by miStudio (producer) and miLLM (server). Both repos test their resolver against every case here, and the cross-repo check keeps this file byte-identical in both. FP32 rows load float32; every other row loads the checkpoint's own 16-bit dtype, falling back to bfloat16 when the checkpoint records float32 or nothing. storage_dtype is how miStudio stores captured activations (bf16 converts to float16 exactly within +-65504; out-of-range values are refused). Change the rule HERE first, then both resolvers. A PRE-QUANTIZED checkpoint (its config carries quantization_config: GPTQ, AWQ, FP8...) keeps the 16-bit rule whatever its row is labelled, because its unquantized modules and the size plan are 16-bit and GPTQ/AWQ kernels at float32 are unsupported.",
